{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>See now, I have two daughters, etc. Only to these men, etc.</b> He exerted himself on behalf of his guests to save them, because they had come under the shadow of his roof; but that he should appease the men of the city by making his daughters free for all — this is nothing but cruelty of heart, for the matter of violating women was not far from his eyes, nor would he, by his own judgment, be committing a great outrage against his daughters. Therefore our Rabbis of blessed memory said: in the normal way of the world a man puts himself forward for his daughters and his wife and kills or is killed — yet this one hands over his daughters to be abused. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: 'For yourself you are guarding them.'" "<b>And know</b> that this matter resembles the concubine at Gibeah, and it is even harsher than that one. For in the case of the concubine at Gibeah, even though they came for the guest, they were silent regarding his concubine; whereas here they would not have been silent when he handed over his daughters. Moreover, there not all the people of the city agreed, whereas here 'from young to old, all the people from every quarter' — thus explained the Ramban, of blessed memory. <b>In Bereshit Rabbah:</b> 'Only to these men' — these are divinities, thus far."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:35.249085132Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}